- 
-+`GIT_TAG "v4.2.0"` pins the FetchContent dependency to the `v4.2.0` release tag so CI and downstream builds use the same revision.
-+
-+`GIT_SHALLOW ON` requests a shallow clone for that tag instead of downloading the repository history.
-+
-+If `GIT_SHALLOW` is omitted, FetchContent performs a full clone, which increases CI time because
-+the checkout has to download the repository history before configuration can continue.
